1	# Developing an Add Operator for the ATB from Scratch
2	
3	This tutorial aims to get you started with the ATB. It does not focus on pursuing performance but strives to enable you to get the results locally within 30 minutes.
4	
5	You can choose to develop new operators in the `ops_customize` directory. This avoids repeatedly building the ATB itself during development, improving your development efficiency. For details, refer to [README_en](https://gitcode.com/cann/ascend-transformer-boost/blob/master/ops_customize/README.md).
6	
7	## ATB Operator Development Deliverables
8	
9	The following figure shows the ATB operator development process:
10	<!--
11	![Operator development process](images/development-process.png)
12	-->
13	### Operator Functionality
14	
15	Two input tensors are added along a specified dimension to produce one output tensor.
16	![AddcustomOperation](images/AddcustomOperation.png)
17	
18	### New Files
19	
20	- Create the `addcustom` directory under `src/kernels/kernels`. This directory stores certain operator implementation code. The specific file contents are described later. The directory structure is as follows:
21	
22	    ```
23	    addcustom
24	    ├── op_kernel                                // Kernel-side implementation files (including the kernel function entry and implementation files)
25	    │   └── addcustom.cpp
26	    ├── tiling                                    // New operator tiling
27	    │   ├── addcustom_tiling.cpp	// Core tiling algorithm
28	    │   ├── addcustom_tiling.h		// Operator tiling interface
29	    │   └── tiling_data.h			// Definition of the tiling_data structure for passing between tiling and the kernel
30	    ├── CMakeLists.txt	                    // CMake file for building the new operator
31	    ├── addcustom_kernel.cpp           // Validation
32	    └── addcustom_operation.cpp             // Shape validation
33	    ```
34	
35	- Create the `addcustom` directory under `src/ops/ops_infer`. This directory stores the code for integrating the addcustom operator into the ATB framework. The specific file contents are described later. The directory structure is as follows:
36	
37	    ```
38	    addcustom
39	    ├── addcustom_operation.cpp          // ATB interface implementation
40	    ├── addcustom_operation.h
41	    ├── addcustom_ops_runner.cpp    // Operator graph
42	    └── addcustom_ops_runner.h
43	    ```
44	
45	- Add the `src/kernels/include/asdops/params/addcustom.h` file to define the parameter structure of the `Addcustom` operation:
46	
47	    ```c++
48	    #ifndef ATBOPS_PARAMS_ADDCUSTOM_H
49	    #define ATBOPS_PARAMS_ADDCUSTOM_H
50	
51	    #include <cstdint>
52	    #include <string>
53	    #include <sstream>
54	    #include <mki/utils/SVector/SVector.h>
55	
56	    namespace AsdOps {
57	    namespace OpParam {
58	    struct Addcustom {
59	        int addcustomDim = 0;
60	
61	        bool operator==(const Addcustom &other) const
62	        {
63	            return this->addcustomDim == other.addcustomDim;
64	        }
65	    };
66	
67	    } // namespace OpParam
68	    } // namespace AtbOps
69	
70	    #endif
71	    ```
72	
73	### Modified Files
74	
75	- Add the new header file `src/kernels/include/asdops/params/addcustom.h` to `src/kernels/include/asdops/params/params.h`.
76	
77	    ```c++
78	    #include "asdops/params/addcustom.h"
79	    ```
80	
81	- `src/kernels/configs/kernels/op_list.yaml` does not exist on first build. After the build, add the following content. This operation is very important as it adds the new operator information to the list. Only then will the implementation and interface of the new operator truly complete in subsequent builds.
82	
83	    ```
84	    AddcustomOperation:
85	        AddcustomKernel:
86	            ascend910b: true
87	     ```
88	
89	- Add the following content to `include/atb/infer_op_params.h`:
90	
91	    ```c++
92	    struct AddcustomParam {
93	        int addcustomDim = 0;
94	        uint8_t rsv[12] = {0};
95	    };
96	    ```
97	
98	- Add the following content to `tests/framework/c++/atb_torch/operation/operation_funcs.cpp`:
99	  - Deserialize the `Addcustom` parameters described in JSON format into a C++ structure, and then use it to create or update the operator:
100	
101	    ```c++
102	    static atb::Status AddcustomOperationCreate(const nlohmann::json &paramJson, atb::Operation **op)
103	    {
104	        atb::infer::AddcustomParam param;
105	        ATB_LOG(INFO) << "AddcustomParam axis:" << param.addcustomDim;
106	        if (paramJson.contains("addcustomDim")) {
107	            param.addcustomDim = paramJson["addcustomDim"].get<int>();
108	        }
109	        if (paramJson.contains("rsv")) {
110	            for (size_t i = 0; i < paramJson["rsv"].size(); i++) {
111	                param.rsv[i] = paramJson["rsv"].at(i).get<int8_t>();
112	            }
113	        }
114	        return CreateOperation(param, op);
115	    }
116	    ```
117	
118	  - Add the corresponding key-value pair to `g_funcMap` in the file.
119	
120	    ```c++
121	    {"AddcustomOperation", &AddcustomOperationCreate},
122	    ```
123	
124	- Add the operator description to `ops_configs/atb_ops_info.ini`.
125	
126	    ```
127	    [AddcustomOperation]
128	    input0.name=x
129	    input0.dtype=int32
130	    input0.format=nd
131	    input1.name=y
132	    input1.dtype=int32
133	    input1.format=nd
134	    output0.name=output
135	    output0.dtype=int32
136	    output0.format=nd
137	    ```
138	
139	- Add the following content to `src/atb/utils/param_to_json.cpp`:
140	
141	    ```c++
142	    template <> nlohmann::json OpParamToJson(const infer::AddcustomParam &opParam)
143	    {
144	        nlohmann::json paramsJson;
145	        paramsJson["addcustomDim"] = opParam.addcustomDim;
146	        return paramsJson;
147	    }
148	    ```
149	
150	## Environment Setup
151	
152	You can refer to [Environment Setup](../README_en.md#2-environment-setup) to set up the build and test environments. Once they are ready, you can begin your ATB operator development journey.
153	
154	## ATB Operator Implementation
155	
156	This process involves operator implementation on the kernel and tiling on the host.
157	
158	### Tiling
159	
160	For core concepts in tiling, such as `TilingData`, `Workspace`, `TilingKey`, and `BlockDim`, refer to the [glossary](https://www.hiascend.com/document/detail/en/CANNCommunityEdition/850alpha001/opdevg/Ascendcopdevg/atlas_ascendc_10_00013.html).
161	
162	#### tiling_data.h
163	
164	File path: `src/kernels/kernels/addcustom/tiling/tiling_data.h`
165	Function: Defines the structure of the block information during data tiling.
166	
167	```c++
168	#ifndef ASCEND_OPS_ADDCUSTOM_TILING_DATA
169	#define ASCEND_OPS_ADDCUSTOM_TILING_DATA
170	
171	#include <cstdint>
172	
173	namespace AsdOps {
174	struct AddcustomTilingData {
175	    uint32_t totalLength;  // Total data length
176	    uint32_t tileNum;      // Number of tiling blocks
177	};
178	}
179	#endif  // ASCEND_OPS_ADD_CUSTOM_TILING_DATA
180	```
181	
182	#### addcustom_tiling.h
183	
184	File path: `src/kernels/kernels/addcustom/tiling/addcustom_tiling.h`
185	Function: This process tiles data. Therefore, the main function is the one that implements the tiling functionality. Here is the function declaration.
186	
187	```c++
188	#ifndef ASCEND_OPS_ADDCUSTOM_TILING_H
189	#define ASCEND_OPS_ADDCUSTOM_TILING_H
190	
191	#include <mki/launch_param.h>
192	#include <mki/kernel_info.h>
193	#include <mki/utils/status/status.h>
194	
195	namespace AsdOps {
196	using namespace Mki;
197	Status AddcustomTiling(const LaunchParam &launchParam, KernelInfo &kernelInfo);
198	} // namespace AsdOps
199	
200	#endif
201	```
202	
203	#### addcustom_tiling.cpp
204	
205	File path: `src/kernels/kernels/addcustom/tiling/addcustom_tiling.cpp`
206	Function: Implements the main function for tiling.
207	
208	```c++
209	#include "addcustom_tiling.h"
210	#include <mki/utils/assert/assert.h>
211	#include <mki/utils/log/log.h>
212	#include <mki/utils/platform/platform_info.h>
213	#include <mki/utils/math/math.h>
214	#include <mki/utils/SVector/SVector.h>
215	#include "asdops/params/addcustom.h"
216	#include "tiling_data.h"
217	
218	// Define the minimum block length.
219	constexpr uint32_t MIN_BLOCK_LENGTH = 1;
220	
221	namespace AsdOps {
222	Status AddcustomTiling(const LaunchParam &launchParam, KernelInfo &kernelInfo)
223	{
224	    AddcustomTilingData *tilingDataPointer =
225	        reinterpret_cast<AddcustomTilingData *>(kernelInfo.GetTilingHostAddr());
226	    MKI_CHECK(tilingDataPointer != nullptr, "tilingDataPtr should not be empty",
227	              return Status::FailStatus(ERROR_INVALID_VALUE, "tilingDataPtr should not be empty"));
228	
229	    if (launchParam.GetParam().Type() != typeid(OpParam::Addcustom)) {
230	        return Status::FailStatus(
231	            ERROR_ATTR_INVALID_TYPE,
232	            "Failed to check addcustom param, type of specificParam is not equals to OpParam::Addcustom");
233	    }
234	
235	    // Obtain the dimension of the input tensor.
236	    const uint32_t totalLength = launchParam.GetInTensor(0).desc.dims.at(0);
237	    MKI_LOG(INFO) << "Total length is " << totalLength;
238	
239	    // Get the number of cores.
240	    uint32_t coreNum = PlatformInfo::Instance().GetCoreNum(CoreType::CORE_TYPE_VECTOR);
241	    MKI_LOG(INFO) << "Core number is " << coreNum;
242	
243	    // Get the number of blocks per core.
244	    uint32_t blockDims = std::min<uint32_t>((totalLength + MIN_BLOCK_LENGTH - 1) / MIN_BLOCK_LENGTH, coreNum);
245	    tilingDataPointer->tileNum = blockDims;
246	    tilingDataPointer->totalLength = totalLength;
247	
248	    MKI_LOG(INFO) << "BlockDims is " << blockDims;
249	    MKI_LOG(INFO) << "Total length is " << tilingDataPointer->totalLength;
250	    MKI_LOG(INFO) << "Tile number is " << tilingDataPointer->tileNum;
251	
252	    kernelInfo.SetBlockDim(blockDims);
253	    return Status::OkStatus();
254	}
255	} // namespace AsdOps
256	```
257	
258	### Kernel Development
259	
260	For concepts related to the kernel, such as `Compute`, `CopyIn`, and `CopyOut`, refer to the [glossary](https://www.hiascend.com/document/detail/en/CANNCommunityEdition/850alpha001/opdevg/Ascendcopdevg/atlas_ascendc_10_00013.html).
261	
262	#### addcustom.cpp
263	
264	File path: `src/kernels/kernels/addcustom/op_kernel/addcustom.cpp`
265	Function: Moves and computes all data based on the tiling information.
266	
267	```c++
268	#include "kernel_operator.h"
269	#include "kernels/utils/kernel/kernel_utils.h"
270	#include "kernels/addcustom/tiling/tiling_data.h"
271	using namespace AscendC;
272	
273	static constexpr uint32_t BUFFER_NUM = 2;
274	static constexpr uint32_t MAX_UB_SIZE = 188 * 1024; // Double buffer, 94 KB per buffer, 188 KB in total
275	
276	class Addcustom {
277	public:
278	    __aicore__ inline Addcustom() {}
279	    __aicore__ inline void Init(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, GM_ADDR z, AsdOps::AddcustomTilingData *tdata)
280	    {
281	        this->totalLength = tdata->totalLength;
282	        this->tileNum = tdata->tileNum;
283	        this->blockLength = totalLength / GetBlockNum();
284	        this->tileLength = blockLength / tileNum / BUFFER_NUM;
285	
286	        // Set the start address and total length of global variables.
287	        xGm.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float *)x, totalLength * sizeof(float));
288	        yGm.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float *)y, totalLength * sizeof(float));
289	        zGm.SetGlobalBuffer((__gm__ float *)z, totalLength * sizeof(float));
290	
291	        // Initialize pipes and queues.
292	        pipe.InitBuffer(inQueueX, BUFFER_NUM, tileLength * sizeof(float));
293	        pipe.InitBuffer(inQueueY, BUFFER_NUM, tileLength * sizeof(float));
294	        pipe.InitBuffer(outQueueZ, BUFFER_NUM, tileLength * sizeof(float));
295	    }
296	    __aicore__ inline void Process()
297	    {
298	        for (int32_t i = 0; i < tileNum; i++) {
299	            CopyIn(i);
300	            Compute(i);
301	            CopyOut(i);
302	        }
303	    }
304	
305	private:
306	    __aicore__ inline void CopyIn(int32_t progress)
307	    {
308	        // Allocate local memory.
309	        LocalTensor<float> xLocal = inQueueX.AllocTensor<float>();
310	        LocalTensor<float> yLocal = inQueueY.AllocTensor<float>();
311	
312	        // Copy data from the global memory to the local memory.
313	        DataCopy(xLocal, xGm[progress * tileLength], tileLength * sizeof(float));
314	        DataCopy(yLocal, yGm[progress * tileLength], tileLength * sizeof(float));
315	
316	        // Enqueue the local memory.
317	        inQueueX.EnQue(xLocal);
318	        inQueueY.EnQue(yLocal);
319	    }
320	    __aicore__ inline void Compute(int32_t progress)
321	    {
322	        // Dequeue the local memory.
323	        LocalTensor<float> xLocal = inQueueX.DeQue<float>();
324	        LocalTensor<float> yLocal = inQueueY.DeQue<float>();
325	        LocalTensor<float> zLocal = outQueueZ.AllocTensor<float>();
326	
327	        // Perform element-wise addition.
328	        Add(zLocal, xLocal, yLocal, tileLength);
329	
330	        // Enqueue the result into the output queue.
331	        outQueueZ.EnQue(zLocal);
332	
333	        // Free the input local memory.
334	        inQueueX.FreeTensor(xLocal);
335	        inQueueY.FreeTensor(yLocal);
336	    }
337	    __aicore__ inline void CopyOut(int32_t progress)
338	    {
339	        // Dequeue the local memory from the output queue.
340	        LocalTensor<float> zLocal = outQueueZ.DeQue<float>();
341	
342	        // Copy the result from the local memory to the global memory.
343	        DataCopy(zGm[progress * tileLength], zLocal, tileLength * sizeof(float));
344	
345	        // Free the local memory.
346	        outQueueZ.FreeTensor(zLocal);
347	    }
348	
349	private:
350	    TPipe pipe;
351	    TQue<QuePosition::VECIN, BUFFER_NUM> inQueueX, inQueueY;
352	    TQue<QuePosition::VECOUT, BUFFER_NUM> outQueueZ;
353	    GlobalTensor<float> xGm;
354	    GlobalTensor<float> yGm;
355	    GlobalTensor<float> zGm;
356	    uint32_t totalLength;
357	    uint32_t tileNum;
358	    uint32_t blockLength;
359	    uint32_t tileLength;
360	};
361	
362	inline __aicore__ void InitTilingData(const __gm__ uint8_t *p_tilingdata, AsdOps::AddcustomTilingData *tilingdata)
363	{
364	    tilingdata->totalLength = ((const __gm__ uint32_t *)p_tilingdata)[0];
365	    tilingdata->tileNum = ((const __gm__ uint32_t *)p_tilingdata)[1];
366	}
367	
368	extern "C" __global__ __aicore__ void addcustom(GM_ADDR x, GM_ADDR y, GM_ADDR z, GM_ADDR tiling)
369	{
370	    Addcustom op;
371	    AsdOps::AddcustomTilingData tdata;
372	    InitTilingData(tiling, &tdata);
373	    op.Init(x, y, z, &tdata);
374	    op.Process();
375	}
376	```
